[spec-invariant-exemptions
  [doc [#
The SPEC-INVARIANT exemption register (RULED: QUAL-1 (d); the SPECINV-1 round).

`make spec-invariant-gate` (scripts/spec_invariants.cx) requires every sentence of
the two rings' approved specs that carries MUST, MUST NOT, SHALL, REFUSES or NEVER
to cite, beside it, a conformance case that grades it. A row here is the only other
way through, and it says WHY no case can: the sentence's spec file, a verbatim
`match=` substring of the sentence (as `--list` prints it, markdown included), one
class of the closed four, and a reason.

  step     a make step grades it, not a corpus case: held-by= names the target
           (it must exist in this repository's or a ring's Makefile)
  author   an obligation on the program author, a binding's author or an
           operator: no implementation behaviour exists to grade
  quoted   the sentence reports or quotes another document's keyword; it is
           not a requirement of this spec
  no-lane  the behaviour is the implementation's, but no corpus lane can feed
           its input: issue= names the open issue that adds the lane

The gate refuses a row that matches no sentence, one whose sentence cites a case
(stale), an unknown class, a missing reason, a held-by= that is no make target, and
a no-lane row without an issue.
#]]

  [; ── the data ring: cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/*.md ── ]

  [; ── abi.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=author match='Bindings MUST read the prefix byte and render diagnostic codes' reason='an obligation on a binding author decoding the cx_validate diagnostic wire; no binding lives in the two rings to grade']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=author match='`program` MUST be non-NULL and non-empty' reason='a precondition on the C caller (a binding author); the sentence states no consequence the library enforces']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#16' sec='cx_code_diagram' match='MUST be non-NULL and non-empty (length 0 yields `CXER0100`)' reason='cx_code_diagram called with source_len 0: a C ABI boundary no corpus lane calls and abi-c-test does not exercise']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#16' sec='cx_code_tree' match='MUST be non-NULL and non-empty (length 0 yields `CXER0100`)' reason='cx_code_tree called with source_len 0: a C ABI boundary no corpus lane calls and abi-c-test does not exercise; it answers an empty-root JSON there, not CXER0100']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=author match='MUST be non-NULL and non-empty.' reason='cx_lint input: a precondition on the C caller (a binding author); the sentence states no consequence the library enforces']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=author match='A binding MUST read `cx_features` from the library it actually loaded' reason='an obligation on a binding author loading the library']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=author match='Decoders without bit 29 MUST reject ast_bin payloads with version byte' reason='obliges a decoder built without capability bit 29 (a binding author); the shipped reader is v10, and the general version refusal is graded by astb-007']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=author match='v7 readers MUST reject v8 files' reason='obliges a reader built at v7 (a binding author); the shipped reader is v10, and the general version refusal is graded by astb-007']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=author match='Decoders without bit 37 MUST raise CXER0100 on tag' reason='obliges a decoder built without capability bit 37 (a binding author); the shipped decoder advertises it and decodes 0x16 (astb-033, astb-034)']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/abi.md' class=author match='decoders without bit 41 MUST reject' reason='obliges a data-bin decoder built without capability bit 41 (a binding author); the shipped decoder advertises it']

  [; ── ast-bin.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/ast-bin.md' class=author match='decoders without bit 37 MUST raise `CXER0100` rather than silently degrading' reason='obliges a decoder built without capability bit 37 (a binding author); the shipped decoder advertises bit 37 and decodes 0x16 (astb-033, astb-034)']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/ast-bin.md' class=author match='MUST request them via the JSON projection (`cx_to_json` with source-tracking enabled)' reason='an obligation on tooling authors consuming ast_bin; the wire carrying no loc is graded by the byte-identical round trips astb-019, astb-022']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/ast-bin.md' class=author sec='MatchNode' match='MUST request them via the JSON projection, not via ast_bin.' reason='an obligation on tooling authors consuming ast_bin; the MatchNode wire carrying no loc is graded by the byte-identical round trips of the MatchNode cases']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/ast-bin.md' class=author match='Tooling that needs source- locations MUST request them via the JSON projection' reason='an obligation on tooling authors consuming ast_bin; the wire carrying no loc is graded by astb-029']

  [; ── ast.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/ast.md' class=author match='Parsers MUST document which they return, and provide a resolver if they return Parse AST' reason='a documentation obligation on a parser implementer; no runtime behaviour to grade']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/ast.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#16' match='Importers MUST reconstruct the TableData payload from this shape' reason='the AST-JSON importer (cx.ast_to_cx) is reachable only through the C ABI cx_ast_to_cx; no CLI format, codec or program verb reads AST-JSON, so no corpus lane can feed it']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/ast.md' class=author match='tooling that needs them MUST request them explicitly' reason='an obligation on tooling that consumes the JSON projection']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/ast.md' class=author match='AST-bin emitters MUST reject PathNode values with `CXER0290` until the wire-format tag is honoured' reason='obliges a binding that has not implemented the v8 codec (a binding author); the shipped emitter honours tag 0x13 (astb-019)']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/ast.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-code#27' match='When the data reader REFUSES and the program reader accepts' reason='the cx --ast dispatch is a CLI projection no corpus lane drives (the document lane parses with the data codec, the program lane evaluates); note the shipped reader reads [$f 1] as an Array with a Hole, so the dispatch never reaches the program tree']

  [; ── canonical.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/canonical.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#18' match='implementations MUST check the AST shape, not the surface' reason='an AttrTest-template predicate cannot be fed: PathNode values exist only as decoded ast_bin, ast-bin.md section 4.1 defines no ProgramExpr tag, and the shipped decoder reads predicates as a String source']

  [; ── lockfile.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/lockfile.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#17' match='Loaders MUST reject any `version` value they do not recognise' reason='the loader rejects it (CXLOCK_UNSUPPORTED_VERSION in lockfile_reader.v) but program cases resolve modules against the runner-fixed cx.lock in stdlib_bundle.v, so no corpus lane can hand the loader a lockfile']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/lockfile.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#17' match='Loaders MUST reject any HTTPS `[module]` entry that lacks an `sri` field' reason='no corpus lane can hand the loader a lockfile; the module world is the runner-fixed cx.lock in stdlib_bundle.v, where every https entry carries an sri']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/lockfile.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#17' match='Loaders MUST accept both and MAY accept additional algorithms' reason='no corpus lane can hand the loader a lockfile pinned with sha256 and with sha384; the runner-fixed cx.lock pins one algorithm']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/lockfile.md' class=author match='MUST be committed to source control' reason='an obligation on the project that owns cx.lock']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/lockfile.md' class=author match='CI MUST NOT auto-regenerate it on every build' reason='an obligation on the operator of a CI pipeline']

  [; ── schema.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/schema.md' class=step held-by=test-vcx-suite match='**none** — export REFUSES' reason='cx schema export is a CLI verb with no program surface; cli_umbrella_test.v test_schema_export_refuses_unprojectable_keys_clause grades the refusal, naming the clause']

  [; ── schema_event_evolution.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/schema_event_evolution.md' class=quoted match='Two approved specs contradict on unknown vocabulary' reason='a finding that quotes the market spec and the identity model, not a requirement of this spec']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/schema_event_evolution.md' class=quoted match='The market spec' reason='a ruling about the market spec downgrade-skip MUST, quoted by name; the requirement lives in the market spec']

  [; ── semantic_value_model.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/semantic_value_model.md' class=author match='The other three senses MUST be named by their row' reason='an obligation on specification authors writing about identity']

  [; ── streaming.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/streaming.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#16' match='MUST be the first event after StartDoc' reason='the read-side event stream is an ABI surface; no corpus lane exposes the events a reader produces']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/streaming.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#16' match='Decoders that encounter an unknown discriminator MUST raise' reason='the event wire decoder is an ABI surface; no corpus lane feeds event bytes']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/streaming.md' class=author match='the synchronous list return MUST be the primary conformance target' reason='an obligation on a binding author choosing its streaming idiom']
  [exempt file='cx-core-data/spec/03-approved/core/streaming.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-data#16' match='have no emit entry point and MUST reject with `W009` at emit time' reason='the streaming-write lane (grading/streaming.v) has ops only for the 14 emittable events, so a case cannot hand the writer an XMLDecl or StartArray; an unknown op is a runner error, not W009']

  [; ── the code ring: cx-core-code core/code.md, core/security.md ── ]
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=step held-by=test-vcx-suite match='fall back to the data reading: a resource that is valid DATA but not a valid PROGRAM evaluates to itself' reason='a host fallback when NO separate data input is supplied; every corpus case runs with one, so no case reaches it — eval_semantics_umbrella_test.v test_streaming_honours_the_data_fallback_like_one_shot (and the CLI runs in diagram_umbrella_test.v) grade it']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=step held-by=test-vcx-suite match='it MUST NOT mask a broken program' reason='the host fallback is unreachable from the corpus (data input always supplied); eval_semantics_umbrella_test.v test_where_infix_eq_fails_loud_not_data_fallback / test_non_name_atom_fails_loud_not_data_fallback / test_program_shaped_lex_failure_fails_loud_not_data_echo run cx FILE and grade it']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=step held-by=test-vcx-suite match='the host MUST surface the original program diagnostic and fail (non-zero exit) instead of falling back' reason='same three eval_semantics_umbrella_test.v CLI tests: a program-intent parse failure exits non-zero with the program diagnostic, never a data echo']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=author match='have at least one fixture in `conformance/code.txt` exercising its happy path' reason='an obligation on the corpus author; no step counts built-in fixtures (check-code-fixtures counts directives and CXER codes only)']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=author match='Any future one MUST iterate in canonical key order' reason='pre-registers a rule for a map-traversal surface that the pure list does not yet carry; no implementation behaviour to grade — and stdlib/map.md declares keys pure in insertion order, the contradiction filed as cx-home/cx-core-code#33']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=author match='`fn` **MUST** be associative' reason='an obligation on the program author; the spec says violations produce undefined results, not a runtime error']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=author match='`z` **MUST** be the identity for `fn`' reason='an obligation on the program author; the spec says violations produce undefined results, not a runtime error']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=step held-by=test-vcx-suite match='the observable output **MUST** match the' reason='the DR-8 bit-for-bit gate: diagram_umbrella_test.v test_code_diagram_output_matches_captured_goldens_bit_for_bit over vcx/tests/testdata/code_diagram_golden']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=step held-by=test-vcx-suite match='Renderers **SHALL** produce structurally equal diagrams across implementations' reason='one reference renderer (cx-stdlib/diagram); a native or second renderer is held to its output by the DR-8 golden gate, diagram_umbrella_test.v test_code_diagram_output_matches_captured_goldens_bit_for_bit']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=author match='Edits that map to valid AST transformations **MUST** round-trip cleanly' reason='conditional on the SHOULD of bidirectional editing: binds a renderer author who ships diagram editing; the reference renderer ships no editing UI']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=author match='reordering positional children of a directive) **MUST**' reason='conditional on the SHOULD of bidirectional editing: binds a renderer author who ships a diagram-editing UI; the reference renderer ships none']
  [exempt file='cx-core-code/spec/03-approved/core/code.md' class=no-lane issue='cx-home/cx-core-code#28' match='Flags **MUST** support' reason='a CLI flag surface no corpus lane can feed; and cx diagram today ignores --direction and --detail and accepts unknown flags (see the report)']
